{
  "id": "diagnostics/headers/09_header_bodies",
  "topic": "diagnostics",
  "subtopic": "headers",
  "title": "Errors in headers' function bodies",
  "summary": "An error inside a function body of a header shows on the file that instantiates it, as the file is edited",
  "prose": "The editor's compile parses the function bodies of the headers a file includes, and instantiates the templates the file uses: an inline function's errors, a template's for the arguments the file instantiates it with, or those of the file's own generic lambda such a template calls, show on the file as it is edited. The parse's own diagnostics come first: the file answers its requests while clang still instantiates, and what the instantiations raise follows.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "#include \"shapes.h\"\n\nstruct Square {\n    int side;\n};\n\nint use() {\n    return area(Square{2}) + unit();\n}\n\nint count() {\n    return apply([](auto value) { return value.size(); });\n}\n",
      "markers": []
    },
    {
      "path": "shapes.h",
      "text": "#pragma once\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nint area(const T& shape) {\n    return shape.width * shape.height;\n}\n\ninline int unit() {\n    return 1;\n}\n\ntemplate <typename F>\nint apply(F f) {\n    return f(1);\n}\n",
      "markers": []
    }
  ],
